  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/c27ff316601ece28946ef45711690d6aabca92a4c35f07b0b1cc1c0982fb5d8e.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=cos\u2061x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-cos\u2061x.$\n\n- Finally, translate it by $1$ unit **up** to give $y=-cos\u2061x+1$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-cos\u2061x+1.$",
